R"VG(
# ending_last.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the last recording (C-12: the latest of a people's records, by its last person at its
# last place: `@cast last`). One a people, so it must be that people's alone: its age's medium, its cause, what its last person sees from
# the door (the people's own houses, herds, crops, sky), what they do with the last day, and how they sign off.

genre.last (words=15..84)
  {@cast last}{last.body}

last.body
  (age=prehistoric) {last.prehistoric}
  (age=medieval) {last.medieval}
  (age=industrial) {last.industrial}
  (age=modern) {last.modern}
  (age=futuristic) {last.futuristic}
  (age=farfuture) {last.farfuture}

# ---- the old time: the last marks on a stone ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

last.prehistoric
  {ann.lp.a} {ann.lp.b} {ann.lp.c}
  {ann.lp.a} {ann.lp.c} {ann.lp.d}
ann.lp.a
  On the last stone, a single figure standing in {colour.holy}, and many figures lying down behind it.
  The last marks of {$home}: one figure, a fire of {fuel}, and the {herd} gone.
  The last figure is painted in {colour.holy}, alone, at the bottom of the wall.
  On the last stone, the {herd} are drawn walking away, and one figure watching them go.
  The last wall shows a figure sitting by {ann.lp.water}, its hands in its lap.
  The last marks are {motif.over}, many, cut over and over, as if someone could not stop.
ann.lp.b
  (has:$me) Beside the standing one, the sign of {$me:name}, inside {motif.over}.
  A hand pressed in {colour.holy} under it, alone.
  Round it, the strokes of a count of the {herd} that stops halfway.
  The fire is drawn very small, smaller than the {bird} on the walls.
ann.lp.c
  Then nothing. The rest of the stone is smooth, kept for {motif.over} that never came.
  After it the wall is bare, and the {colour.holy} stops.
  (has:$me) The ship reads the sign as {$me:name}, and after it only the {game}.
  There is room for more {motif.over}, and there are none.
ann.lp.d
  {last.cause.pic}
  The {game} are drawn going over the hill, and nobody after them.
ann.lp.water
  (desert=1) a dry hole
  (desert=0) the water
  a fire gone out

# ---- the medieval: a writing set in a wall -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

last.medieval
  {ann.lm.a} {last.cause} {ann.lm.b} {ann.lm.c}
  {ann.lm.a} {ann.lm.b} {last.cause} {ann.lm.d}
ann.lm.a
  I am the last at {$home}, and the {herd} are mine now.
  (has:$me) I, {$me:name}, write this at {$home} by a fire of {fuel}, being the last.
  No child was born at {$home} this year, or last, and no {herd} either.
  I am old and the {craft} is done and nobody will need it.
  This is set in the wall of {holyplace} at {$home} by the last hand, under {motif.over}.
ann.lm.b
  The {ann.houses} on the hill stand empty; I keep the gate open in case, and the {herd} wander in.
  I set this in the wall, under {motif.over}, so that someone knows the {people} were here.
  The {herd} come to the door in the evening, and I give them what there is.
  I have swept {holyplace} every morning and lit {fuel} there; it is clean, if nobody comes.
  I eat {food} and drink {drink} and talk to the {beast}.
  The {crop} came up by itself in the old fields this year. Nobody cut it.
ann.lm.c
  We were here, with our {herd} and our {crop}. {god}, we were here.
  {god}, you kept {city} {#year|year}. Keep the {tree}, keep {river}, keep the {herd}. They were always more yours than ours.
  {god.keep}, whoever you are.
  Let this be found, and the {colour.holy} cloth with it.
  The rest is for {god} to finish, and the {bird}.
ann.lm.d
  I will {rite.imp} once more, and then I will sit down.
  Tomorrow I will go up to {deadplace} and lie down with the rest.
  When this is set, I will close the gate after all, and let the {herd} out.


# ---- the industrial age: spoken into the machine, or left on the table --------------------------------------------------------

last.industrial
  {ann.li.a} {last.cause} {ann.li.b} {ann.li.c}
  {ann.li.a} {ann.li.b} {last.cause} {ann.li.c}
ann.li.a
  (has:$me) This is {$me:name}, at {$home}, by the {fuel} stove.
  (inv.railway=1) The last train left {$home} {n} years ago with the last of the {crop}.
  (has:$me) My name is {$me:name}, I was a {$me.trade}, and as far as I know I am the last at {$home}.
  If this cylinder is played, someone is listening over the {vessel}. Good.
  I am writing this on the back of a notice about the {crop} price, because there is no other paper.
ann.li.b
  There is nobody to send this to, so I am speaking it into the machine by the {fuel} stove.
  I wind the clock at the station every morning and feed the {herd} after; somebody should.
  The works are quiet. I go and stand among the {craft} benches sometimes, because I am used to the noise.
  The {herd} have the run of the streets now, and they are welcome to them.
  I light {fuel} in one room and live in it.
  The pictures on the walls are of people I knew, in their {garment.n:pl}. I talk to them.
ann.li.c
  If the machine outlasts me, it will have been worth the {ann.cointrouble}.
  That is all, and a {vessel.one.n} of {drink} to see me out.
  Goodnight, {$home}.
  {god.keep}, whoever plays this.

# ---- the modern age: a recording, a broadcast to nobody -------------------------------------------------------------------------

last.modern
  {ann.lmo.a} {last.cause} {ann.lmo.b} {ann.lmo.c}
  {ann.lmo.a} {ann.lmo.b} {last.cause} {ann.lmo.c}
ann.lmo.a
  (has:$me) This is {$me:name}. It's the {#year:ord} year of {city}, I'm the last one at {$home}, and I'm out of {food}.
  Testing, testing: this is {$home}, calling anyone, from under the {roofs}.
  (has:$me) {$me:name} again. Day {n}. Still here, still eating {food}.
  If you're hearing this, the batteries lasted longer than I did, and the {herd} too.
ann.lmo.b
  The lights still come on at night over {streets.of}. I leave them on.
  Nobody has answered in {n} days. I'll keep calling, between the {herd} and the {crop}.
  I walked to the end of {streets.of} today and back. Nobody.
  The {herd} got out of somebody's yard. They're living in the square now. I feed them.
  I made {food} for one and ate it on the roof.
  I put on the old music and danced the {~dance}, badly, by myself.
ann.lmo.c
  If anyone is out there and sees the lights on the {roofs}, that's us. That was us.
  I'll try again tomorrow, {time.of}.
  Over. Nobody to say over to. Over anyway, with {drink} in my hand.
  Goodnight, whoever. Feed the {herd} if you come.

# ---- the futuristic age: a personal record the machines keep ---------------------------------------------------------------------

last.futuristic
  {ann.lf.a} {last.cause} {ann.lf.b} {ann.lf.c}
  {ann.lf.a} {ann.lf.b} {last.cause} {ann.lf.c}
ann.lf.a
  (has:$me) Personal record of {$me:name}, {$home}, the last of the {ann.craftfolk}.
  (has:$me) {$me:name}, at {$home}.
  Record for whoever comes; this is {$home}, under {skyone}.
  The machines asked me to say something for the record, over my {drink}, so this is it.
ann.lf.b
  I am the last one awake. The {ann.houses} are lit and empty.
  The machines will keep this; I asked them to keep it, and the {herd}, until someone comes.
  The gardens are in perfect order, the {fruit} ripe. Nobody needs them.
  The machines still set a place for everyone at dinner, with {food}; I asked them to stop, and then I asked them to start again.
  I spent the morning on the roof, watching {skyone}.
  The {herd} the machines keep for us are fat and do not know anything has happened.
ann.lf.c
  They said they would, and swore it {oath}. They always kept their word, which is more than we did.
  I am going to sit by the window over the {crop} until it gets dark, and then I am going to keep sitting.
  End of record. There will not be another one, unless the {bird} learn to speak.
  Look after the machines and the {herd}. They looked after us.

# ---- the far future: the last record of the people --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

last.farfuture
  {ann.lff.a} {last.cause} {ann.lff.b}
  {ann.lff.a} {ann.lff.c} {last.cause} {ann.lff.b}
ann.lff.a
  (has:$me) This is the last record of the {people}, made at {$home} by {$me:name}, in {colour.mourn}.
  This is the last record of the {people}, made under {skyone}.
  Here the {people} end, at {$home}, among the {tree}, without fear.
  The last of the {people} speaks, under {motif.over}.
ann.lff.b
  There is a word for what we feel now, our {~word}, and the machine will not carry it across; goodbye, whoever you are.
  We are not sad; please do not be sad for us, or for the {herd}.
  We put out the lights ourselves and left the {colour.holy} one burning. It seemed polite.
  Everything is in order, the {vessel} sealed, the {craft} finished.
ann.lff.c
  We have kept {festival} one last time, with {feast.custom}, all of us that are left.
  {focusword} will stand after us. It was built for that.
  We said the names of everyone, to {instrument}, which took a long time.

# ---- the cause, as the last one says it --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

last.cause
  (cause=drying) {watersrc} is sand at the bottom.
  (cause=drying) The last of the water is in {vessel.one}, and it is not enough.
  (cause=sickness|cause=greatsickness|cause=epidemics|cause=engineered) The sickness took the rest, and the {herd} with them.
  (cause=sickness|cause=greatsickness|cause=epidemics|cause=engineered) I have marked every door in {colour.any} but my own.
  (cause=famine|cause=cropfailure|cause=foodsystems) There was not enough {crop}, at the end, for anyone.
  (cause=famine|cause=cropfailure|cause=foodsystems) The {vessel} are empty and the {herd} are gone.
  (cause=iceage|cause=cold) The snow is at the window and the {fuel} is gone.
  (cause=iceage|cause=cold) The {fuel} ran out in {season.now}, and the cold came in.
  (cause=flood|cause=climate) The water is at the door and over the {crop}.
  (cause=flood|cause=climate) The lower town is under {river} now, and the rest will follow.
  (cause=bandwar|cause=civilwar|cause=conquest|cause=industrialwar|cause=waterwar) The fighting is over. Nobody is left to fight over the {crop} or the {herd}.
  (cause=conquest) The {other} have the rest. They have not come up the hill yet.
  (cause=leaving|cause=exodus|cause=elsewhere) Everyone else went; I stayed with the {herd}.
  (cause=leaving|cause=exodus|cause=elsewhere) They went to {dest}, all of them, and did not send word.
  (cause=volcanic|cause=impact) The sky has been grey for years, and the {crop} with it.
  (cause=poisoned|cause=coalout|cause=revolution|cause=cascade) Nothing works any more.
  (cause=nuclear|cause=weapons) The fire took the cities and the {crop}.
  (cause=fewerchildren|cause=chosen) There were no children after us, only the {herd}.
  (cause=machine|cause=retreat) The others went into the machines and left me the {herd}.
  (cause=nanotech|cause=geoengineering|cause=flare) The land is dead outside, even the {tree}.
  (cause=physics|cause=undescribed) What happened cannot be said, not even in {~word}.
  (cause=sunlost) The sun went, and then the warmth, and then the others, down to {hall.below} and further.
  (cause=sunlost) There is no sun to see this by. I write it by {kept.light}, at {warm.ground}.
  (cause=sunlost) The stars are out at noon, as they have been for {#darkyears|year}, and the cold is at the door of {hall.below}.
last.cause.pic
  (cause=drying) A {watersrc.n} drawn with a cross over it.
  (cause=sickness|cause=greatsickness|cause=epidemics|cause=engineered) Figures drawn lying in rows, with red spots on them.
  (cause=famine|cause=cropfailure|cause=foodsystems) Empty bowls drawn in a line.
  (cause=iceage|cause=cold) White dots over everything.
  (cause=flood|cause=climate) Wavy lines over the huts.
  (cause=bandwar|cause=civilwar|cause=conquest|cause=industrialwar|cause=waterwar) Spears drawn broken.
  (cause=leaving|cause=exodus|cause=elsewhere) Footprints going away.
  (cause=volcanic|cause=impact) A grey sky over everything.
  (cause=sunlost 4) A small circle drawn high up, and under it the figures going into a hole in the ground.
  (cause=sunlost 4) The sun drawn smaller and smaller along the wall, and then a blank stone.
  A great many figures lying down among the {herd}.
ann.cointrouble
  trouble
  {fuel}
  paper
)VG"
